lso started a Copernicus workflow\nfor procedural materials like Substance Designer.\n\nIts advantage is staying\ninside the same software.\n\nI will see how far Copernicus can go\ncompared with Substance Designer.\n\nAcross my existing components,\nI identified the material tags.\n\nThose tags assign materials\ndirectly to the geometry.\n\nI chose four materials from\nmy concept art and reference images.\n\nNext is the Karma XPU lookdev render.\nThe complete graph is already set up.\n\n/Users/zenray/Downloads/tmp-shorts-vestibule-louisiana-bayou/audio/every-dawn-and-dusk-30s.mp3 cette musique va pour lui /Users/zenray/Downloads/tmp-shorts-vestibule-louisiana-bayou/turntable-ecran-30s.mov\n\net l'autre musique de 30 sec va avec l'autre vidéo de 30 sec /Users/zenray/Downloads/tmp-shorts-vestibule-louisiana-bayou/vestibule-ecran-30s.mov\n\n\ngo n'oublie les animations des sous titres et le nouveaux style des sous titres\n/wait-validation"}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"d580aa3d-2c5d-4d0b-8dfa-e2ac84d3ef91","timestamp":"2026-09-12T16:09:29.513Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"5f649d7d-3f0b-4e40-9aeb-39c6fa2e2eab","version":"2.1.266","gitBranch":"main"}
